# Seed documents for scripts/seed_knowledge_assistant.py are real Office
# binaries (ZIP-based), never text. Without this, a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true (a common default) rewrites line-ending bytes inside the
# ZIP structure and silently corrupts the file - it would still "upload"
# successfully (upload_file only checks the HTTP response), just as garbage
# bytes knowledge-service's parser then fails on or indexes nonsense from.
*.docx binary
*.doc binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
